diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: Access port VLAN membership on switch1 (Campus 1 access switch), specifically interface eth2 (PC5’s access port).
- Mechanism: PC5’s frames are being placed in VLAN 1 instead of VLAN 10, so ARP requests for its default gateway 172.16.10.254 (which lives in VLAN 10) never reach the gateway. Other hosts (PC6/PC7/PC8) are correctly in VLAN 10, so their traffic traverses the trunk to mswitch0 and reaches the gateway normally.
